id: pm-vcs-h8x2
title: Named remotes and remote-tracking refs
description: "A repository can name other repositories and remember where each one's branches were the last time they were observed. Remotes live in their own file rather than in config.json: config.json holds settings that shape history itself (which paths are records, how their fields merge) and must therefore be identical in every clone, whereas the set of remotes is local to one clone and differs between agents. Remote-tracking refs live under refs/remotes/<remote>/<branch> so a fetch can never publish a remote's branch into the local branch namespace."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:vcs",distribution
